  "about": "Quick switcher matching and keyboard conversation stepping, run by every client's tests. match: the query is trimmed and loses one leading # or @; both sides are lowercased and compared by Unicode scalar. Equal 1000, prefix 900, at a word start (after a character that is not a letter or digit) 800, anywhere 700. Otherwise a leftmost greedy subsequence scores 100, +10 per character right after the previous match, +5 per character at a word start, -1 per character skipped, clamped to 1..699; null when the characters do not all appear in order. An empty query scores 0. An item scores its best text (name, then alternates). rank: items that match, by score plus 50 when unread, highest first, then in list order. adjacent: from `current` (null when no listed conversation is open), the next (forward) or previous item, wrapping, never returning `current`; with unreadOnly only unread items count; null when there is none.",
